# Official Qwen block-scaled FP8 checkpoint. Sole surviving Qwen3.8-27B variant on gx10 as of
# 2026-09-02: the unsloth NVFP4 quant (qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4) and the bf16 original (qwen3.8-27b)
# were both removed the same day after this FP8 checkpoint validated as the better choice.
#
# Validated 2026-09-02, two stability-battery runs (cold + warm), both all_passed=true:
#   - Decode: ~22.9 tok/s cold-start, ~26.9-31.9 tok/s warm (no spec-decode; concurrency=4,
#     512in/128out benchmark). CUTLASS FP8 GEMM path (vLLM auto-disables DeepGEMM on Blackwell;
#     forcing it back on via VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=1 + CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a is untested on GB10's
#     specific SM variant and has a known crash mode on the neighboring SM120 -- not attempted).
#   - MMLU (62 subtasks, 5-shot limit, n=310): 0.842-0.874 -- strong, expected range for this
#     model size.
#
# WHY FP8 over the removed NVFP4 sibling despite NVFP4 being faster (67.8-74.3 tok/s): MTP
# spec-decode (k=3), which the NVFP4 recipe required for that speed, was found to badly corrupt
# loglikelihood/logprob-based scoring on this model+vLLM combo -- MMLU collapsed to ~0.45 (barely
# above the 0.25 random floor) with spec-decode ON vs ~0.84-0.89 OFF, reproduced on BOTH v0.27.1
# and v0.28.0 (vLLM PR #51812's GDN-gate/spec-token alignment fix, hoped to fix this, did not --
# v0.28.0 measured 0.362 on vs 0.892 off, if anything worse). This FP8 config runs with SPEC_ARG/
# COMPILE_ARG explicitly cleared (no MTP) specifically to avoid that bug -- do not re-enable
# spec-decode on this model family without first re-verifying logprob correctness, not just
# throughput.
#
# EXTRA_ARGS added 2026-09-02: --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --performance-mode interactivity.
# From live introspection of vLLM v0.28.0's resolved config for this exact model (not just
# --help text): default max-num-batched-tokens resolves to 2048 for us (the changelog's 8192-
# 16384 global bump doesn't reach our config path) -- at 2048 a 256K-token document prefills in
# ~128 scheduler iterations; 8192 cuts that to ~32, targeting the long-context reading use case.
# performance-mode=interactivity only changes cudagraph capture granularity (confirmed via
# source: finer capture sizes, ~76 PIECEWISE + 60 FULL vs the default 51/35), explicitly built to
# favor low per-request latency at small batch sizes -- matches actual usage (mostly single-
# request agentic/chat, not high concurrency). Both confirmed independent/non-conflicting and
# accuracy-neutral (no dtype/kernel-backend change). Validated: cold MMLU 0.874, warm MMLU 0.871,
# both all_passed=true -- matches the pre-change 0.842-0.892 range, no regression. Throughput on
# the 512in/128out/c=4 stability benchmark was flat (~24-27 tok/s, within existing run-to-run
# noise) since that benchmark doesn't exercise long-context prefill or low-concurrency latency --
# the actual targets of these flags -- so no throughput claim is made here, only accuracy-safety.
# DeepGEMM/CuteDSL kernel backends and --kv-cache-memory-bytes were evaluated and NOT adopted:
# DeepGEMM is explicitly auto-disabled by vLLM itself for this model_type on Blackwell ("E8M0
# scale format causes accuracy degradation for this architecture" -- vLLM's own log message, not
# speculation); kv-cache-memory-bytes has no upside over the validated 0.85 gpu-memory-utilization
# fraction. --kv-cache-dtype alternatives (fp8_e4m3, nvfp4, turboquant_*, etc.) remain untested --
# a real lever but needs its own isolated MMLU-gated A/B before adopting, not bundled here.

# --- UI metadata ---
UI_LABEL="Qwen3.8-27B-FP8"
UI_DESC="Official Qwen block-scaled FP8 checkpoint. No spec-decode (MTP k=3 corrupts logprob/loglikelihood scoring on this model family, confirmed on v0.27.1 and v0.28.0 -- see header). Tuned for long-context + low-concurrency: --max-num-batched-tokens 8192, --performance-mode interactivity. ~30.9GB, native 256K context, CUTLASS FP8 GEMM path (DeepGEMM auto-disabled by vLLM for this architecture). Validated 2026-09-02: full stability battery passed twice (cold+warm), MMLU 0.871-0.874, ~24-32 tok/s decode -- the accuracy-safe default for this model."
UI_SIZE="~30.9 GB · FP8 block-scaled · vision · 256K ctx"
UI_SPEED="~24-32 tok/s (measured 2026-09-02, tuned for long-context/low-concurrency, not raw throughput)"
UI_USE_CASES="Vision Q&A, Long-context (256K) reading, Agentic tool-use"
EXPERIMENTAL="0"

# --- Serve recipe ---
SERVE_MODEL="Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8"
SERVED_NAME="qwen3.8-27b-fp8"
SERVE_CONTAINER="swap-vllm-qwen3.8-27b-fp8"
SERVE_PORT="8002"
MAX_LEN="262144"
GPU_UTIL="0.85"
QUANT="fp8"
TOOLS="1"
REASONING_PARSER="qwen3"
KV_ARG=""
GENCFG_ARG=""
EXTRA_ARGS="--max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --performance-mode interactivity"
SPEC_ARG=""
COMPILE_ARG=""
